IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`
IMPORT `pip-part3-required-period`
IMPORT `pip-part5-rates`
IMPORT `pip-part6-age`

-- Tests of Part 5 (regulation 24) and Part 6 (regulations 25 to 27). Expected values were worked out by hand
-- from the text before the file was run.

§ `Tests of regulation 24`

#ASSERT `reg 24(1)(a): the weekly standard rate of the daily living component, in pounds` EQUALS 76.70
#ASSERT `reg 24(1)(b): the weekly enhanced rate of the daily living component, in pounds` EQUALS 114.60
#ASSERT `reg 24(2)(a): the weekly standard rate of the mobility component, in pounds` EQUALS 30.30
#ASSERT `reg 24(2)(b): the weekly enhanced rate of the mobility component, in pounds` EQUALS 80.00
#ASSERT `reg 24: the weekly rate, in pounds, of this component at this rate` `the daily living component` `at` `the standard rate of the component` EQUALS JUST 76.70
#ASSERT `reg 24: the weekly rate, in pounds, of this component at this rate` `the daily living component` `at` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS JUST 114.60
#ASSERT `reg 24: the weekly rate, in pounds, of this component at this rate` `the mobility component` `at` `the standard rate of the component` EQUALS JUST 30.30
#ASSERT `reg 24: the weekly rate, in pounds, of this component at this rate` `the mobility component` `at` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS JUST 80.00
-- No rate of a component: the text prescribes no amount.
#ASSERT `reg 24: the weekly rate, in pounds, of this component at this rate` `the daily living component` `at` `no rate of the component` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 24: the weekly rate, in pounds, of this component at this rate` `the mobility component` `at` `no rate of the component` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests of regulation 25`

#ASSERT `reg 25(b): the claim made before the relevant age qualifies` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(b): the claim made before the relevant age qualifies` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(b): the claim made before the relevant age qualifies` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(b): the claim made before the relevant age qualifies` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 25: one of the two exceptions applies` TRUE `or` FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 25: one of the two exceptions applies` FALSE `or` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25: one of the two exceptions applies` FALSE `or` FALSE)
-- (reached the relevant age, entitled on the day before, the claim qualifies)
#ASSERT `reg 25: section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 25: section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25: section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25: section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

§ `Tests of regulation 26`

#ASSERT `reg 26(1): the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26(1): the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26(1): the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 26(2)(a): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26(2)(a): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` FALSE)
-- "2 years" read as "1 year".
#ASSERT `reg 26(2)(b): the number of years in regulation 15(1)(b)` TRUE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `reg 26(2)(b): the number of years in regulation 15(1)(b)` FALSE EQUALS 2
-- Severely limited ability: the enhanced rate only if C had it; else the standard rate if C had that.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate of the mobility component C is entitled to on the new claim` TRUE `severely limited ability` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `the enhanced rate of the component`
#ASSERT `reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate of the mobility component C is entitled to on the new claim` TRUE `severely limited ability` `the standard rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `the standard rate of the component`
#ASSERT `reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate of the mobility component C is entitled to on the new claim` TRUE `severely limited ability` `no rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `no rate of the component`
-- Limited ability: the standard rate only if C had the component at either rate.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate of the mobility component C is entitled to on the new claim` TRUE `limited ability` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `the standard rate of the component`
#ASSERT `reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate of the mobility component C is entitled to on the new claim` TRUE `limited ability` `the standard rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `the standard rate of the component`
#ASSERT `reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate of the mobility component C is entitled to on the new claim` TRUE `limited ability` `no rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `no rate of the component`
-- Neither level: no rate.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate of the mobility component C is entitled to on the new claim` TRUE `neither limited ability nor severely limited ability` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS JUST `no rate of the component`
-- Regulation 26(1) does not apply: these paragraphs say nothing.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate of the mobility component C is entitled to on the new claim` FALSE `severely limited ability` `the enhanced rate of the component` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests of regulation 26A`

#ASSERT `reg 26A(1): the exceptions of regulation 26A(2) apply` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26A(1): the exceptions of regulation 26A(2) apply` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26A(1): the exceptions of regulation 26A(2) apply` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 26A(2)(a): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26A(2)(a): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 26A(2)(b): the number of years in regulation 15B(1)(b)` TRUE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `reg 26A(2)(b): the number of years in regulation 15B(1)(b)` FALSE EQUALS 2

§ `Tests of regulation 27`

-- reg 27(1): reached the relevant age, entitled under an exception in reg 25 or 26, award falls to be revised or superseded.
#ASSERT `reg 27(1): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply on the revision or supersession` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(1): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply on the revision or supersession` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(1): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply on the revision or supersession` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(1): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply on the revision or supersession` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- A date after the day C reached the relevant age (1 January 2020): the day itself is not after it.
#ASSERT `reg 27(2): the date is after the day C reached the relevant age` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 2)) `than` (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2): the date is after the day C reached the relevant age` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) `than` (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2): the date is after the day C reached the relevant age` (JUST (YMD 2019 12 31)) `than` (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2): the date is after the day C reached the relevant age` NOTHING `than` (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT `reg 27(2)(a): the supersession is for a change of circumstances after the relevant age` TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 2)) (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2)(a): the supersession is for a change of circumstances after the relevant age` TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2)(a): the supersession is for a change of circumstances after the relevant age` FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 2)) (YMD 2020 1 1))

-- reg 27(2), Scottish Ministers version: (mobility component in the award, reg 23, change date, reg 26(1)(a), day C applied, day the Scottish Ministers initiated, day C reached the relevant age)
#ASSERT `reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE TRUE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT `reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1)) NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT `reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1)) (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2019 6 1)) (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1)) (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1)) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1))
-- reg 27(2), Secretary of State version.
#ASSERT `reg 27(2) (Secretary of State version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT `reg 27(2) (Secretary of State version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1)) (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT `reg 27(2) (Secretary of State version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1)) NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2) (Secretary of State version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2) (Secretary of State version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(2) (Secretary of State version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT `reg 27(2A): the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` EQUALS "the Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment, Jobseeker's Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Decisions and Appeals) Regulations 2013"

-- reg 27(3): (original rate, proposed rate, same condition)
#ASSERT `reg 27(3): the Secretary of State may award this rate of the mobility component` `the standard rate of the component` `to replace` `the standard rate of the component` `with` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 27(3): the Secretary of State may award this rate of the mobility component` `the standard rate of the component` `to replace` `the standard rate of the component` `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An original standard rate: never the enhanced rate, whatever the condition.
#ASSERT `reg 27(3): the Secretary of State may award this rate of the mobility component` `the standard rate of the component` `to replace` `the enhanced rate of the component` `with` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 27(3): the Secretary of State may award this rate of the mobility component` `the standard rate of the component` `to replace` `the enhanced rate of the component` `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 27(3): the Secretary of State may award this rate of the mobility component` `the enhanced rate of the component` `to replace` `the enhanced rate of the component` `with` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 27(3): the Secretary of State may award this rate of the mobility component` `the enhanced rate of the component` `to replace` `the enhanced rate of the component` `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An original enhanced rate and a proposed standard rate: the text says nothing.
#ASSERT `reg 27(3): the Secretary of State may award this rate of the mobility component` `the enhanced rate of the component` `to replace` `the standard rate of the component` `with` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 27(3): the Secretary of State may award this rate of the mobility component` `no rate of the component` `to replace` `the standard rate of the component` `with` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- reg 27(4): previous award of the mobility component ceased no more than 1 year before the day the supersession takes effect.
#ASSERT `reg 27(4): entitlement under the previous award is treated as if it were under the original award` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 6 10) (YMD 2025 6 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(4): entitlement under the previous award is treated as if it were under the original award` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 6 9) (YMD 2025 6 10))
#ASSERT `reg 27(4): entitlement under the previous award is treated as if it were under the original award` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 10) (YMD 2025 6 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(4): entitlement under the previous award is treated as if it were under the original award` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 27(4): entitlement under the previous award is treated as if it were under the original award` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10))
